From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Norman Herms <dockseed@proton.me>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 08:29:10 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: allwinner: a733: Add the SMHC1 controller

The SoC dtsi describes SMHC0 and SMHC2, but not SMHC1, the SD/SDIO
controller whose pins go to the 15-pin header J6 of the Cubie A7S.

Add SMHC1 at 0x04021000 with the compatible pair of SMHC0: the manual
gives it the register set of SMHC0, and sunxi-mmc handles it with the A733
configuration. Its bus gate, module clock and reset come from the CCU; the
bus gate's parent is the STORE AHB gate that the controller needs for its
register access. Add the pin groups for PG0 (CLK), PG1 (CMD) and PG2 to
PG5 (D0 to D3), function 2, with the drive strength and pull-up of the
SMHC0 groups. Nothing else uses PG0 to PG5 on the board, so the node
carries them. It is disabled; a board enables it.

Not covered: the 1.8 V signalling and the supplies, which belong to the
board; the pin bank supply, which the pin controller does not switch for
bank PG.

Tested on Radxa Cubie A7S: with the node enabled in a copy of the DTB,
the controller probes and initializes and takes PG0 to PG5; no card was
connected.

Assisted-by: LLM
---
 .../arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733.dtsi | 36 +++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 36 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733.dtsi
index 726171bfe6b8..334d5880d32f 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733.dtsi
@@ -551,6 +551,24 @@ mmc0_3v3_pins: mmc0-3v3-pins {
 				power-source = <3300000>;
 			};
 
+			/omit-if-no-ref/
+			mmc1_clk_pin: mmc1-clk-pins {
+				pins = "PG0";
+				allwinner,pinmux = <2>;
+				function = "mmc1";
+				drive-strength = <30>;
+				bias-pull-up;
+			};
+
+			/omit-if-no-ref/
+			mmc1_pins: mmc1-pins {
+				pins = "PG1", "PG2", "PG3", "PG4", "PG5";
+				allwinner,pinmux = <2>;
+				function = "mmc1";
+				drive-strength = <10>;
+				bias-pull-up;
+			};
+
 			/* RST and CLK */
 			mmc2_clk_rst_pins: mmc2-clk-rst-pins {
 				pins = "PC1", "PC5";
@@ -1044,6 +1062,24 @@ mmc0: mmc@4020000 {
 			#size-cells = <0>;
 		};
 
+		mmc1: mmc@4021000 {
+			compatible = "allwinner,sun60i-a733-mmc",
+				     "allwinner,sun20i-d1-mmc";
+			reg = <0x04021000 0x1000>;
+			interrupts = <GIC_SPI 162 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_HIGH 0>;
+			clocks = <&ccu CLK_BUS_MMC1>, <&ccu CLK_MMC1>;
+			clock-names = "ahb", "mmc";
+			resets = <&ccu RST_BUS_MMC1>;
+			reset-names = "ahb";
+			pinctrl-names = "default";
+			pinctrl-0 = <&mmc1_pins>, <&mmc1_clk_pin>;
+			max-frequency = <200000000>;
+			cap-sd-highspeed;
+			status = "disabled";
+			#address-cells = <1>;
+			#size-cells = <0>;
+		};
+
 		mmc2: mmc@4022000 {
 			compatible = "allwinner,sun60i-a733-emmc",
 				     "allwinner,sun50i-a100-emmc";
